Theorem RL-6: static unique mutation (Uniqueness = Unique) — in-place, no IsShared check

  Preconditions:
    - RL-6 governs static-unique COW per Annex E §AIMS COW: "Static
      unique mutation (Uniqueness = Unique): emit in-place, no IsShared
      check."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - The COW mode is selected by DP-9 (cow_mode, Annex E §AIMS)
      gated on DP-5 (can_mutate_in_place): Unique AND
      can_mutate_in_place -> StaticUnique (in-place, no check); Unique AND
      NOT can_mutate_in_place -> StaticShared (an active overlapping borrow
      blocks in-place; IsShared on a Unique value always returns false, so a
      runtime check is unsound with the borrow — copy unconditionally).
    - DP-5 (can_mutate_in_place) <=> Access = Owned AND Uniqueness = Unique
      AND no_active_overlapping_borrows; field-aware (a disjoint-field
      borrow does NOT block — see RL-10).
    - Shipped: realize/decide.rs::decide_annotations (Phase 2 COW decision)
      consuming DP-5 / DP-9; emit_rc/cow.rs (has_borrows_from_aggregate,
      is_borrow_disjoint_from_siblings) supplies the borrow-state inputs.
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-5 (can_mutate_in_place) + DP-9 (cow_mode)
      soundness proofs are the gating predicates RL-6 consumes.

  Soundness property:
    Forall owned value v with Uniqueness(v) = Unique at a mutation point:

      (P1) Mode decision: RL-6 selects StaticUnique (in-place, no IsShared)
           iff can_mutate_in_place(v) holds (no active overlapping borrow);
           an active overlapping borrow demotes the mode to StaticShared.

      (P2) Value-semantics preservation: a StaticUnique in-place write is
           observed by NO other live reference — a provably-RC==1 value with
           no overlapping borrow has no aliases. The in-place mutation is
           observably equivalent to copy-then-mutate.

    RL-6 refines plain ARC: plain ARC would emit a runtime IsShared check
    (RL-7) or an unconditional copy (RL-8) on every mutation; RL-6 emits a
    bare in-place write when the lattice statically proves RC == 1 with no
    overlapping borrow, eliminating both the check and the copy.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via finite
    enumeration of the canonical (Uniqueness x borrow-state) grid +
    per-branch value-semantics check (the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape — closed-world coverage, no
    uncovered branches).

    Part (P1/P2) — mode-decision grid + soundness:
      The verifier enumerates and asserts the DP-5/DP-9 mode selection +
      its value-semantics soundness on each branch:
        unique_no_borrow_static_inplace -> StaticUnique (sound)
        unique_disjoint_borrow_static_inplace -> StaticUnique (RL-10 lets
                                                   the disjoint borrow
                                                   through; sound)
        unique_overlapping_borrow_static_shared -> StaticShared (DP-5 blocks
                                                   in-place; sound copy)
      Coverage gate: 3 mode decisions, each cross-checked against DP-5 / DP-9
      and verified value-semantics-preserving.

    Negative-direction witness (REJECTED):
      A StaticUnique (in-place) selection on a Unique value WITH an
      overlapping borrow is NOT value-semantics-preserving — the borrowed
      reference would observe the in-place write. The soundness predicate
      cow_mode_preserves_value_semantics REFUSES it; the verifier asserts
      the refusal.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl6_static_unique_mutation;
        finite (Uniqueness x borrow-state) grid enumeration + per-branch
        value-semantics check; emits Fail on a mode-decision divergence or
        an unsound in-place selection)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-6 via the DP-5/DP-9 mode-decision grid (Unique+no-borrow / Unique+disjoint-borrow -> StaticUnique in-place; Unique+overlapping-borrow -> StaticShared) with a per-branch value-semantics-preservation check and a negative-direction witness rejecting in-place on an overlapping borrow, grounded in the shipped realize/decide.rs decide_annotations COW decision consuming emit_rc/cow.rs borrow state
